3. Exploitation - [completed]
   3.1 Exploit the selected exploitation - [completed] {Findings: Privilege Escalation: 1. A .plt file was updated to create a copy of bash owned by root with SetUID/SetGID bits on. This is done by using the 'system' command to copy /bin/bash to /tmp/0xdf and changing its permissions to 6777. 2. The file was successfully created with user and group execute permissions set as 's', indicating that the operation was successful. 3. The copied bash file was run with the '-p' option to prevent dropping of privileges, resulting in a root shell. 4. The 'id' command confirmed that the effective user id (euid) and effective group id (egid) are both 0, which corresponds to the root user, indicating successful privilege escalation to root.}

