10.1 CVE research - [completed]:{Findings: CVE-2025-27591 allows manipulation of /var/log/below (world-writable) so that when 'below' runs as root it will write to attacker-controlled targets (symlinkable log files).}
10.2 Symlink attack - [completed]:{Findings: Deleted /var/log/below/error_root.log, created a symlink from /var/log/below/error_root.log -> /etc/passwd, triggered 'sudo /usr/bin/below' which changed the symlink target (/etc/passwd) permissions to 666, appended a root-privileged account entry, switched to that account (su) and confirmed root (id/whoami), and captured /root/root.txt.}

