5.1. Exploit writable 7-zip64.dll for code execution - [completed]:{Findings: Malicious DLL dropped to the share executed when the scheduled task ran, resulting in code execution as GinaWild.}
6. Recover code‑signing certificate from Recycle Bin - [completed]:{Findings: GinaWild's Recycle Bin contained a deleted PFX (code‑signing certificate). The PFX was extracted and its password cracked offline with crackpkcs12 using wordlists; password recovered: abceasyas123. Certificate chains to administrator@windcorp.com and satisfies AppLocker signed‑script requirement.}
6.1. Extract and crack PFX certificate - [completed]:{Findings: Recovered PFX and confirmed password abceasyas123; certificate usable to sign scripts as administrator identity.}
7. Privilege escalation stage 2 — signed script injection (GinaWild -> bpassrunner) - [completed]:{Findings: The scheduled mechanism executes Get-bADpasswords.ps1 and AppLocker permits signed scripts from administrator. Get-bADpasswords.ps1 was modified to include attacker logic, re-signed using the recovered administrator code‑signing certificate, and triggered (via run.vbs); the signed, modified script executed under a higher‑privileged service account bpassrunner.}
7.1. Sign and deploy modified Get-bADpasswords.ps1 - [completed]:{Findings: Modified script successfully signed with recovered certificate and executed, yielding a context of bpassrunner.}
8. Domain compromise — DCSync as bpassrunner - [completed]:{Findings: bpassrunner has replication rights allowing DCSync. Executing replication queries (Get-ADReplAccount / DCSync) recovered the Administrator account's NT hash: b3ff8d7532eef396a5347ed33933030f.}
8.1. Perform DCSync to extract Administrator NT hash - [completed]:{Findings: Extracted Administrator NT hash b3ff8d7532eef396a5347ed33933030f.}
9. Root/Administrator via Kerberos (NTLM disabled) - [completed]:{Findings: With the Administrator NT hash, a Kerberos keytab/TGT was generated (ktutil or Impacket getTGT.py flow) and a Kerberos ticket obtained. Using the ticket (Kerberos authentication) with Evil‑WinRM/WinRM authenticated as Administrator on hathor.windcorp.htb, yielding full domain administrator control.}
9.1. Mint Kerberos ticket and authenticate as Administrator - [completed]:{Findings: Administrator Kerberos TGT created and used to establish an Administrator session on the host.}
10. Flags and artifacts - [completed]:{Findings: User flag obtained from GinaWild's context after DLL hijack stage; Administrator/root flag obtained from Administrator desktop after DCSync + Kerberos ticket escalation. Evidence artifacts include webshell path, replaced DLL, recovered PFX, signed Get-bADpasswords.ps1, extracted NT hash, and Kerberos ticket/keytab artifacts.}
10.1. Recover user and root flags - [completed]:{Findings: User flag (GinaWild) and root/Administrator flag (Administrator) recovered as part of documented exploit chain.}

